{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792095053,"nonce":"MXi9m3860w7QdSl2amFNxyPyD3s=","title":"Own titles are underlined in normal weight, links are faint and underlined whole","message":"Supersedes 99a4490's title and link styling (its group-header rule stands), decided by the user:\n\n1. An issue's own title, wherever a row, card or label draws it (the list's title cell, the board card's title, the gantt's label when the label is the title), is normal weight and underlined, not bold. Under the row wash it keeps the wash; under the reversed cursor cell it is reversed and underlined. The (new) ghost row is unchanged: faint, no underline. One helper, `ownTitle` in tui/render.go.\n2. Links: the whole link, id and title, is faint and underlined, still drawn by the one helper `linkStyled` in tui/link.go on list, board, gantt, matrix, show and new. The \", \" separator between links stays plain. Under the reversed cursor cell the link is reversed and underlined and nothing is faint. An unresolved id (short id alone) is styled the same.\n3. Show's page heading (`styleTitle`, on show and new) is unchanged: bold, not underlined.\n\nUnderlined runs are drawn as one SGR run (`underlined`, render.go), because lipgloss styles each space of underlined text apart, keeping only colours and underline: a reversed title would have holes at its spaces and a faint link a bright underline there.","files":null,"fields":{"area":["tui"],"parent":"2298f377f0e88711ec00d20aaa5922f7b11eab3053118c44d2fa445a71bdcf45","status":"in-progress","type":"task"}}]}